.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
.Dd October 11, 2026
.Dt DTFL_INPUT_SESSION_NEW 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm dtfl_input_session_new ,
.Nm dtfl_input_session_to_collection ,
.Nm dtfl_input_session_update ,
.Nm dtfl_input_session_update_at ,
.Nm dtfl_input_session_insert ,
.Nm dtfl_input_session_remove ,
.Nm dtfl_input_session_advance_to ,
.Nm dtfl_input_session_time ,
.Nm dtfl_input_session_flush ,
.Nm dtfl_input_session_close
.Nd feed a differential dataflow collection
.Sh LIBRARY
Timely and differential dataflow library
.Pq libdtfl , \-ldtfl
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In dtfl/collection.h
.Ft dtfl_input_session *
.Fn dtfl_input_session_new "const dtfl_type *type" "const dtfl_diff *diff"
.Ft dtfl_collection *
.Fn dtfl_input_session_to_collection "dtfl_input_session *s" "dtfl_scope *scope"
.Ft void
.Fn dtfl_input_session_update "dtfl_input_session *s" "const void *record" "size_t len" "const void *change"
.Ft void
.Fn dtfl_input_session_update_at "dtfl_input_session *s" "const void *record" "size_t len" "const uint64_t *at" "const void *change"
.Ft void
.Fn dtfl_input_session_insert "dtfl_input_session *s" "const void *record" "size_t len"
.Ft void
.Fn dtfl_input_session_remove "dtfl_input_session *s" "const void *record" "size_t len"
.Ft void
.Fn dtfl_input_session_advance_to "dtfl_input_session *s" "const uint64_t *t"
.Ft const uint64_t *
.Fn dtfl_input_session_time "const dtfl_input_session *s"
.Ft void
.Fn dtfl_input_session_flush "dtfl_input_session *s"
.Ft void
.Fn dtfl_input_session_close "dtfl_input_session *s"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
An input session batches differential collection updates and ships them
to a timely dataflow input under coarsened capabilities, which exposes
more concurrency than the logical times suggest.
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_input_session_new
creates a session over records of
.Fa type
with differences of class
.Fa diff ,
retaining both.
.Fn dtfl_input_session_to_collection
adds the session's input to
.Fa scope ,
whose time class must be totally ordered, and returns the collection it
feeds.
It may be called once per session, and the session's epoch starts at the
scope's minimum time.
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_input_session_update
adds
.Fa change
to the weight of
.Fa record
at the current epoch;
.Fn dtfl_input_session_update_at
does the same at a future time
.Fa at ,
which must not precede the epoch.
.Fn dtfl_input_session_insert
and
.Fn dtfl_input_session_remove
are shorthands that add and retract one copy of a record, and need a
diff class with a unit value
.Pq and an Abelian class for remove .
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_input_session_advance_to
moves the epoch to
.Fa t ,
which must not precede the current epoch; it does not inform timely
dataflow until the next flush.
.Fn dtfl_input_session_time
returns the current epoch.
.Fn dtfl_input_session_flush
sends every buffered update into the input and advances the input's
frontier to the epoch; it must be called before expecting the dataflow
to report progress.
.Fn dtfl_input_session_close
flushes, seals the input and frees the session.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn dtfl_input_session_new
returns a new session owned by the caller.
.Fn dtfl_input_session_to_collection
returns the collection the input feeds.
.Fn dtfl_input_session_time
returns the current epoch, or
.Dv NULL
before the session is added to a scope.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
dtfl_diff *r = dtfl_diff_i64();
dtfl_input_session *in = dtfl_input_session_new(dtfl_type_u64(), r);
dtfl_collection *c = dtfl_input_session_to_collection(in, scope);
unsigned char key[8];
uint64_t next = 1;

dtfl_put_u64(key, 42);
dtfl_input_session_insert(in, key, sizeof key);
dtfl_input_session_advance_to(in, &next);
dtfl_input_session_flush(in);
/* ... step the worker until the probe passes `next` ... */
dtfl_input_session_remove(in, key, sizeof key);
dtfl_input_session_close(in);
dtfl_collection_free(c);
dtfl_diff_free(r);
.Ed
.Sh ERRORS
These functions report contract violations through the panic hook: a
time that does not advance the epoch, a diff class that lacks the unit
value or negation that
.Fn dtfl_input_session_insert
and
.Fn dtfl_input_session_remove
need, or a scope whose time class is not totally ordered.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr dtfl_collection_new 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_execute 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_input_new 3 ,
.Xr dtfl 7
.Sh HISTORY
This is the C form of differential dataflow's
.Vt InputSession
and the
.Vt Input
trait of
.Pa input.rs .
.Sh THREAD SAFETY
An input session and the collection it returns belong to the worker
thread that created them and must not be shared.
Each worker in a multi-worker computation builds its own session.
